.\" robodr-blackbox(1). Source of truth: the USAGE text in
.\" crates/robodr-blackbox/src/bin/robodr-blackbox.rs. Keep the two in sync.
.TH ROBODR\-BLACKBOX 1 "2026-10-16" "RoboDR 0.1.0-alpha.1" "RoboDR Manual"
.SH NAME
robodr\-blackbox \- create black\-box keys, verify and inspect RoboDR black\-box logs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B robodr\-blackbox keygen
.B \-\-out
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-key\-id
.IR ID ]
.PP
.B robodr\-blackbox verify
.I DIR
.B \-\-keyring
.I FILE
.RB [ \-\-keyring
.IR FILE ]...
.RB [ \-\-checkpoint
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-device
.IR ID ]
.RB [ \-\-strict ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.PP
.B robodr\-blackbox inspect
.IR DIR | SEGMENT
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-limit
.IR N ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The RoboDR black box is an append\-only, hash\-chained, signed log of evidence
records split into segment files. This tool manages its keys and checks logs.
Secrets are never accepted on the command line (argv is readable by every
process through
.IR /proc ).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B keygen
Write a new HMAC\-SHA256 key file
.RI ( robodr\-blackbox\-key/v1 ,
JSON) to
.IR FILE .
32 bytes are drawn from
.IR /dev/urandom ;
the command fails rather than fall back to weaker randomness. The file is
created exclusively with mode 0600; an existing file or symlink is never
overwritten or written through. Without
.BR \-\-key\-id ,
the key id is derived from the key. Prints the key id, never the secret.
.TP
.B verify
Verify the log in
.I DIR
with every key in the given key or keyring files
.RI ( robodr\-blackbox\-keyring/v1 ),
so a log that spans a key rotation verifies. Key files that are symlinks, not
regular files, or accessible by group or others are refused.
.B \-\-checkpoint
names a trusted checkpoint held off the unit; without it the directory's own
.I checkpoint.json
is used.
.B \-\-device
requires the chain's device id.
.B \-\-strict
also fails on warnings (for example a recovered torn tail).
.B \-\-json
prints the full report as JSON.
.TP
.B inspect
List the frames of a log directory or of one segment file (sequence number,
kind, flags, time, payload preview), at most
.I N
with
.BR \-\-limit .
No signature is checked: it is a viewer, not a verdict.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; for
.BR verify :
intact (warnings allowed unless
.BR \-\-strict ).
.TP
.B 1
Verification failed (tampering, or warnings with
.BR \-\-strict ).
.TP
.B 2
Usage, I/O or key error, including an argument that is not valid UTF\-8.
.SH NOTES
HMAC\-SHA256 is a placeholder authenticator: whoever holds the key can verify
and also forge evidence. Keep exactly one copy on the robot and one in the
verifier's protected store.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR robodr\-agentd (8),
.BR robodr\-replay (1),
.BR robodr\-diode\-unpack (1),
/usr/share/doc/robodr/OPERATIONS.md
